==Galician==
[[File:Ferrol City.jpg|thumb|''Ría'' de Ferrol / Ferrol bay]]
[[File:Ría de Ortigueira desde la sierra de A Capelada.jpg|thumb|''Ría'' de Ortigueira / Ortigueira bay]]

===Etymology 1===
Attested since 1432. From {{m|gl|río||river}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|gl|[ˈri.ɐ]}}

====Noun====
{{gl-noun|f}}

# {{lb|gl|geography}} Geographical coastal [[landform]] where a river [[valley]] is partially subducted under the sea level; similar to a [[firth]], although usually translated into English cartography as [[bay]]
#: {{syn|gl|abra|esteiro}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1448|editor=A. López Ferreiro|title=Fueros municipales de Santiago y de su tierra|location=Madrid|publisher=Ediciones Castilla|page=560
|passage='' o dito seu lugar e vila da Proba ena '''ria''' dela''
|translation=said place and town of A Pobra [do Caramiñal] in its '''bay'''}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1460|author=Rui Vasques|title=Crónica de Santa María de Iria|location=Santiago|publisher=Ediciós do Castro|page=135
|passage=''Et logo comesçou a rreparrar o castello do Est por gardar a terra dos ysmaelitas et normanos, que entrauã porla '''rria''' e estragauã toda a terra.''
|translation=And then he began to repair the castle of Oeste, for protecting the country from the Ismaelites and the Norsemen, who used to enter through the '''bay''', then wasting all the land}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|gl|da ría|t=locally [fished]}}

